{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430173-hit-and-run","id":430173,"title":"Hit and Run","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-06T06:28:14-08:00","id":430173,"title":"Hit and Run","content":"Under Gift of Evasion (Purity) on page 124.<br /> <br /> &quot;This Facet can be used to interrupt an attack action that is aimed at the Uratha. Before the action is taken, the Uratha may immediately disengage and move up to her full Speed away. This alone may foil an attack, but if she is able to move to a location that takes her out of line-of-sight of all of her prey, she then rolls the Facet\u2019s dice pool against the highest Composure of those prey who could previously see her. The Uratha can only interrupt one action per turn in this way.&quot;<br /> <br /> A reflexive gift that costs of 1 Essence. Is it me, or is this basically &quot;one extremely cheap perfect defense per turn that also has a chance to render you immune to all other attacks until the beginning of your next turn&quot;? I understand that, to an extent, Werewolves are <i>suppossed</i> to brutally win combat and crush everything underneath, but this Facet seems to completely negate one on one combat as being a thing (unless both people have this Facet, in which case it becomes a game of wiffing until someone runs out of Essence). If the whole Pack has it (likely) then it negates Pack vs Single Giant Epic Monster storylines as well. Unless the Giant Epic Monster attacks with explosions or doesn't need line of sight.<br /> <br /> Am I reading this facet wrong or missing something? If not, has this come up in playtest and how did it work out at the actual table?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:31:11-08:00","id":430191,"title":"","content":"I thought it only worked if you had yet to act and used said action. (ima go reread)<br /> <br /> Yeah... I'm thinking I 'added' the whole use your action bit. My gut says its not as powerful as it seems as it only grants a move action with a potential penalty to perception, wits and intelligence rolls (as opposed to Celerity's instant interrupt) and costs an Essence each time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","user":"Gnomish American","date":".  I reread. 03-06-2015, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:52:51-08:00","id":430213,"title":"","content":"Prey A punches Werewolf B. Werewolf B activates Hit and Run and moves a few feet backwards. Does Prey A's attack automatically miss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:56:28-08:00","id":430217,"title":"","content":"Pretty much, but that's no different from celerity, same cost even.... OH! its limited by celerity dots... yeah this could be problematic. Make sure you put this in the Errata thread. Should it not be addressed my fix'll be limiting its uses to the Uratha's Purity Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:02:35-08:00","id":430222,"title":"","content":"It also can't be negated by surprise, which Celerity can and is a pretty huge balancing point. I don't think this is an &quot;Errata&quot; issue so much as a &quot;Balance&quot; issue. Again, assuming I'm not missing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:02:39-08:00","id":430223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430173-hit-and-run#post430173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under Gift of Evasion (Purity) on page 124.<br /> <br /> &quot;This Facet can be used to interrupt an attack action that is aimed at the Uratha. Before the action is taken, the Uratha may immediately disengage and move up to her full Speed away. This alone may foil an attack, but if she is able to move to a location that takes her out of line-of-sight of all of her prey, she then rolls the Facet\u2019s dice pool against the highest Composure of those prey who could previously see her. The Uratha can only interrupt one action per turn in this way.&quot;<br /> <br /> A reflexive gift that costs of 1 Essence. Is it me, or is this basically &quot;one extremely cheap perfect defense per turn that also has a chance to render you immune to all other attacks until the beginning of your next turn&quot;? I understand that, to an extent, Werewolves are <i>suppossed</i> to brutally win combat and crush everything underneath, but this Facet seems to completely negate one on one combat as being a thing (unless both people have this Facet, in which case it becomes a game of wiffing until someone runs out of Essence). If the whole Pack has it (likely) then it negates Pack vs Single Giant Epic Monster storylines as well. Unless the Giant Epic Monster attacks with explosions or doesn't need line of sight.<br /> <br /> Am I reading this facet wrong or missing something? If not, has this come up in playtest and how did it work out at the actual table?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're not reading it wrong. In playtests it wasn't particularly troublesome, especially given the Urhan capabilities all Uratha have. Giant Epic Monsters can, among other things, often reach quite far. Still, it's worth noting; I thought I had added the same limitations onto it as Celerity has, but apparently not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430173-hit-and-run?p=430213#post430213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prey A punches Werewolf B. Werewolf B activates Hit and Run and moves a few feet backwards. Does Prey A's attack automatically miss?</div> </div> </div> </div>It misses if the werewolf has moved far enough that the prey's attack can no longer connect, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430173-hit-and-run?p=430217#post430217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much, but that's no different from celerity, same cost even.... OH! its limited by celerity dots... yeah this could be problematic. Make sure you put this in the Errata thread. Should it not be addressed my fix'll be limiting its uses to the Uratha's Purity Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, not adding the Celerity-style limitation to the number of uses per scene was an oversight. Using Purity dots as the limiter works fine for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:09:25-08:00","id":430228,"title":"","content":"I would definitely consider adding in the unaware thing as well, if you are trying to make it equal to Celerity. That's arguably a more important balance point then the limited uses per scene. Technically speaking, Hit and Run needs &quot;Once interrupted, the other character must continue his declared action, if it\u2019s still possible. If the action is no longer possible, he takes no action&quot; in there somewhere to function clearly as intended. Otherwise, if you have both books one would deduce that the attacker can opt to just do something else. I would also recommend adding in, &quot;Alternatively, that character\u2019s player may declare his action a dramatic failure and take a Beat.&quot; from Celerity simply because, from my experience, it makes players feel better about being autododged when it's used against them.<br /> <br /> I would assume that &quot;Likewise she cannot move further in a single turn than her Speed would allow.&quot; is deliberately left out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:13:35-08:00","id":430231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430173-hit-and-run?p=430228#post430228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would definitely consider adding in the unaware thing as well, if you are trying to make it equal to Celerity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that should be the goal. Especially as Acrozatarim pointed out, werewolf deal with epic monsters and even regular monsters that vampires don't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:19:55-08:00","id":430239,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Hit and Run is its own thing, but the only-use-it-Purity-dots-times-per-scene seems a pretty reasonable limiter to put on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:18:12-08:00","id":430295,"title":"","content":"A more thematic limitation might be to say, &quot;This facet may only be activated on a turn in which the Werewolf has landed a damaging attack against the interrupted adversary.&quot;<br /> <br /> That way you solve the ambush beating problem, and get the <b>hit</b> part of hit and run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:54:43-08:00","id":430355,"title":"","content":"I'm confused... &quot;if she is able to move to a location that takes her out of line-of-sight of all of her prey, she then rolls the Facet\u2019s dice pool against the highest Composure of those prey who could previously see her. The Uratha can only interrupt one action per turn in this way.&quot; What happens if she succeeds? What happens if she fails?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-06-2015, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T10:52:46-08:00","id":430440,"title":"","content":"That's described later in the Facet. I didn't copypaste the whole thing deliberately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T11:22:50-08:00","id":430457,"title":"","content":"Oh, that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T13:53:57-08:00","id":430567,"title":"","content":"They get the Shadow Paranoia Condition for a number of turns equal to the Werewolf's Purity renown. This makes them sort of on edge and jumping at shadows, which are full of enemies slavering for their flesh. A -2 penalty to Perception, if they make a failure with it, it's an automatic dramatic failure and they see something out of the corner of their eye and react accordingly. There's also a penalty to Intelligence and Wits rolls, as the paranoia keeps them from thinking rationally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T13:57:08-08:00","id":430571,"title":"","content":"Yep, Hit &amp; Run and Shadow of the Predator both give ways of getting Shadow Paranoia onto prey. Shadow of the Predator has the benefit that you can do it without them knowing you're there and in a more targeted fashion, while Hit &amp; Run comes with a disengage power attached.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:22:37-08:00","id":430605,"title":"","content":"Succeeding on Hit and run also makes them lose track of you, so you hide, setting up an ambush for next action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}